{
  "purpose": "Innioasis Y1 (MT6572) overlays on Linux 6.18.56; none of the Y2 set. MT6572 drivers backported from mt6572-mainline/linux 8d427adfb611bcdf4326efc69f44a23c14871b20 (based on Linux 7.0-rc7); docs/planning/Y1-SECOND-BOOT-PLAN.md, Y1-THIRD-BOOT-PLAN.md, Y1-CHARGING-PLAN.md, Y1-DISPLAY-PLAN.md, Y1-BACKLIGHT-PLAN.md, Y1-AUDIO-PLAN.md, Y1-POWER-PLAN.md (0030: the Y2's power-off patch 0027, unchanged), Y1-REBORN-PLAN.md (0031: the MT6572 GPU power domain; 0032: the Y2's Lima patch 0038, unchanged; 0033: an optional label names the PMIC key device; an optional hold reports KEY_POWER on a second device), Y1-DATA-PLAN.md (0034: the eMMC write guard), Y1-MTP-PLAN.md (0035: the Y2's musb_ep_start, a freshly queued request is served from the FIFO). Y1-BLUETOOTH-PLAN.md (0036/0037: the MT6572 connectivity owner, built but without a DT node; the Y2's btif.c, stp.c, hci.c, firmware.c and protocol.h shared unchanged).",
